-- title:
--   Regular one-dimensional fibre modulo varpi_S from the completion
-- statement:
--   Let $R'$ be a commutative ring that is a regular local ring, let $\varpi', \tau \in R'$ be elements whose span is the whole maximal ideal, $\mathfrak m_{R'} = (\varpi', \tau)$, and assume the Krull dimension of $R'$ is $2$. Let $S$ be a commutative ring that is local and noetherian, and let $\varpi_S \in S$. Suppose given a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_S$-adic completion of $S$ onto the $\mathfrak m_{R'}$-adic completion of $R'$, carrying the image of $\varpi_S$ under the canonical map $S \to \widehat S$ to the image of $\varpi'$ under the canonical map $R' \to \widehat{R'}$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions about the quotient of $S$ by the principal ideal generated by $\varpi_S$: that $S/(\varpi_S)$ is a regular local ring, and that its Krull dimension equals $1$. Here Krull dimension is taken with values in the extended integers, so the dimension hypothesis and conclusion are equalities $\operatorname{dim} R' = 2$ and $\operatorname{dim} S/(\varpi_S) = 1$ in that ordered set.
--
--   This is the descent step which transfers regularity of a two-dimensional regular local ring, with a chosen regular system of parameters one of which is $\varpi'$, across an isomorphism of adic completions, so as to recognise the fibre $S/(\varpi_S)$ as a regular curve-like local ring. It is used in the analysis of fibres of modular curves at full level, in the verification that such a fibre is a regular local ring once ramification away from a section is controlled.
